<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>SecureBank | Login</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
</head>
<body class="auth-body">
  <div class="bg-orb orb-1"></div>
  <div class="bg-orb orb-2"></div>
  <div class="bg-grid"></div>

  <main class="auth-layout">
    <section class="hero-panel glass">
      <div class="brand-row">
        <div class="brand-logo">SB</div>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Final Project Demo</p>
          <h1>SecureBank Security Lab</h1>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="hero-text">
        This demo shows external CSRF, stored XSS + CSRF, and compares
        defense strategies across Low, Medium, and High security levels.
      </p>

      <div class="feature-list">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-icon">⚠️</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Low</h3>
            <p>No effective CSRF protection. External attacker page can steal money.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-icon">🛰️</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Medium</h3>
            <p>Origin / Referer validation blocks the external attacker page.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-icon">🛡️</span>
          <div>
            <h3>High</h3>
            <p>Origin / Referer validation plus CSRF token on the transfer form.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-icon">💥</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Stored XSS + CSRF</h3>
            <p>A malicious script inside the bank page can bypass stronger defenses.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="auth-card glass">
      <div class="auth-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Welcome back</p>
        <h2>Sign in to continue</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          Use one of the demo accounts below.
        </p>
      </div>

      <% if (error) { %>
        <div class="alert alert-error"><%= error %></div>
      <% } %>

      <form action="/login" method="POST" class="auth-form">
        <label class="input-group">
          <span>Username</span>
          <input type="text" name="username" placeholder="Enter username" required />
        </label>

        <label class="input-group">
          <span>Password</span>
          <input type="password" name="password" placeholder="Enter password" required />
        </label>

        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-full">Login</button>
      </form>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>